{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3661","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3661","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3661\",\"parent_revision\":\"a8a9387dfbcff0dc49d0fce616db568080e8eedd1eb6a4f9e5c75c8104c744ea\",\"root_revision\":\"a8a9387dfbcff0dc49d0fce616db568080e8eedd1eb6a4f9e5c75c8104c744ea\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-19\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nIssue #3060 received 18 or more comments of 70,000 to 190,000 characters each on 2026-09-19, each a full-item snapshot (`dh-work-item-version`) written by the backlog backend during one groom. `gh api repos/Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills/issues/3060/comments` shows comment bodies of 89,052, 91,931 and 111,484 characters in the last three alone.\\n\\nImpact: the issue's comment thread is dominated by machine snapshots, which hides the human decisions recorded as comments on the same issue; every `gh issue view --comments` read and every reader of the issue pays for megabytes of snapshot text; each groom write adds another snapshot.\\n\\nRelated: #2573 (sync redesign), which does not mention these comments.\\n\\n**Hypothesis**: the GitHub backend stores each item version as an issue comment (the audit-comment record `backlog_view`'s `refresh` description mentions), and every section write creates a new one.\\n\\nExpected: an item's version history does not grow the issue's human comment thread by a full-item copy per write.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation, re-groom of #3060, 2026-09-19\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-19\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"cbb2bf733dead9085acd914d397a5f4917fbdb88f7cffaaae7e9407ec172835d\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVoHmow\"}"}